    CRF: less MSRP churn + seamless transient recovery; pin seed 7 (good USB)
    
    Two CRF robustness fixes (researched against GenAVB_TSN MRP/MSRP, the authoritative
    NXP reference; avdecc/jdksavdecc are AVDECC-only, no MSRP):
    
    1) srp.c — on a RECEIVED LeaveAll (RLA), restart our own LeaveAll timer instead of
       also originating one. 802.1Q Table 10-5 / GenAVB mrp.c:1234-1237: only one
       participant per segment should source LeaveAlls. We were double-originating,
       doubling segment-wide re-declaration churn; every LeaveAll forces the MOTU
       talker to re-declare, and a slow re-declare is a window where the CRF can gap.
    
    2) main.c — AAF talker gate for cs=1 now keys on mcr.bound (CRF still PATCHED),
       not the instantaneous mcr.servo_locked. On a transient CRF stall the stale
       watchdog holds the NCO at gptp_locked_base (= the GM/MOTU 48 kHz), so audio
       keeps flowing at the correct rate through the ~1-3s self-heal instead of muting.
       Explicit unpatch unbinds -> mutes, so "no CRF = no audio" holds. No harsh tone:
       the NCO is never at an unverified CRF rate.
    
    Diagnosis (from the on-HW log): SRP was healthy (talker_reg=1, our_fail=0) at the
    CRF stale, and the stale watchdog reads on-wire frames via the HW CRF extractor,
    so the ~1s gap was frames physically stopping (external MacBook-wake/MOTU
    transient), not our reservation aging out. Our MSRP is already more-than-compliant
    (LeaveAll handling + 1s periodic Join). Fix 1 reduces churn; Fix 2 makes any
    residual transient inaudible.
    
    avb_soc.py — pin --seed default 7. The firmware change re-rolled placement; seeds
    4/5 stalled HeAP, seed 6 placed but its intra-region USB placement was marginal
    (bad USB FIFO) despite fine global Fmax. Seed 7 places AND has HW-verified good
    USB. Global sys Fmax does NOT predict USB — re-sweep + HW-test after firmware
    changes.
    
